  "x-decisions": {
    "architecture": "One application and one database; feature-oriented packages, controllers, application services, repositories, entities and DTOs. Do not expose JPA entities. Avoid unnecessary abstraction.",
    "stack": "Java 21, Spring Boot 3.5.16, Maven 3.9.16 with Wrapper 3.3.4, Spring Web, Bean Validation, Spring Data JPA, PostgreSQL, Flyway, JUnit, Testcontainers and springdoc 2.9.1. Other dependency and plugin versions are managed by the Boot parent.",
    "schemaOwnership": "Flyway owns the schema; Hibernate ddl-auto=validate, never update. Released migrations remain unchanged.",
    "time": "Persist timestamptz; compare Java Instant values in UTC; configure UTC. Input timestamps must be ISO-8601 strings with explicit offsets; reject numeric timestamps. Truncate to microsecond precision before window validation, overlap checks and persistence; responses use the same precision in UTC Z. Original input timezone is not retained.",
    "identity": "UUID IDs, including registration IDs. Emails are not unique.",
    "validation": "Nonblank names, location and valid nonblank emails, capacity > 0, startTime < endTime; past sessions allowed. Invalid UUIDs and offset-free timestamps return 400.",
    "publicCoachName": "Keep the name API field through internal first_name/last_name expansion.",
    "nameSplit": "For coaches, normalize ASCII whitespace identically in Java and SQL (space, tab, LF, VT, FF, CR), trim surrounding spaces, first word -> first_name, remainder -> last_name; a single word has empty last_name. Keep the public name API field, recomposed from split fields. Names are normalized at creation, legacy writes and backfill. This is a pragmatic, culturally imperfect policy; participants are unchanged.",
    "migrationCompatibility": "V3 retains legacy name, backfills canonical names and first_name/last_name without changing IDs, emails or relations, then requires non-null split fields. A BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE trigger handles legacy-only and split-only writes. Detect actual UPDATE changes with IS DISTINCT FROM; if both representations are supplied/changed, require equality after normalization or reject with SQLSTATE 23514. Split writers provide both fields, including empty last_name for single names; nulls remain invalid. Canonicalize the composed full name and split by first word. Email-only updates leave names untouched. Old readers continue using name; new JPA maps only split fields. Keep V3 when rolling back the application. Defer dropping name/compatibility triggers until old versions and rollback dependencies retire. V1/V2 remain immutable.",
    "errors": "Stable code and readable message; optional fieldErrors; never disclose stack traces. Generic 500 for unexpected errors.",
    "documentation": "All Markdown including working notes lives in ignored docs/. Reviewer-required README and migration ADR availability must be resolved before submission; do not silently override the owner preference.",
    "git": "Branch exactly ticket ID; Conventional Commits include ticket ID. Commit locally only; owner performs push. No PR creation or remote operations in JBC-001.",
    "outOfScope": [
      "authentication",
      "frontend",
      "notifications",
      "payments",
      "recurring sessions",
      "coach/participant update and delete endpoints"
    ],
    "testing": "Prioritize business logic and HTTP integration tests backed by PostgreSQL. No dedicated Flyway or migration-only tests, per owner scope adjustment in JBC-004. Flyway continues to apply and validate migrations on normal application startup.",
    "localRuntime": "docker compose up --build builds the JAR inside a Java 21 builder and starts a non-root Java 21 runtime with PostgreSQL. GET /actuator/health returns 200 with status UP once the application and database are healthy. PostgreSQL data is stored in a named volume.",
    "ci": "PRs targeting main and pushes to main run Maven verify with Java 21 and PostgreSQL Testcontainers on Ubuntu 24.04. Cache only dependencies; never skip tests. Upload Surefire/Failsafe reports on failure. Require the Maven verify status check in main protection to enforce the merge gate; workflow alone does not enforce it.",
    "schedulingConcurrency": "Within one transaction, lock the coach row with PESSIMISTIC_WRITE before checking existing.start < proposed.end AND existing.end > proposed.start and inserting the session. The lock also covers empty schedules and is held through commit. Every session creation uses this path; direct database writes bypass this application guarantee. Different coaches lock different rows.",
    "sessionFiltering": "Optional coachId/from/to combine with AND. Match endTime > from and startTime < to for supplied bounds, after truncating bounds to microseconds. Either bound may be omitted; from >= to returns 400. Unknown coaches match no sessions. Empty query parameter values follow standard Spring conversion and are treated as omitted. Sort by startTime then UUID; unpaginated array. One read-only database query fetches sessions and coaches; no resource-existence lookup is needed.",
    "registrationCreation": "One transaction checks session, participant, duplicate and capacity in that order, then saveAndFlush returns the generated registration ID. Duplicate takes precedence even when full. Translate only the named uq_registrations_session_participant constraint violation to DUPLICATE_REGISTRATION and roll back; unrelated failures use the sanitized generic 500 handler. The existing V2 unique constraint prevents duplicate pairs, while baseline count/check/insert does not prevent concurrent capacity overflow. Concurrent capacity protection remains optional JBC-017; no new locks or migration in JBC-009.",
    "registrationLifecycle": "Participant listing returns id/name/email/registrationId ordered by participant UUID, with [] for existing empty sessions and 404 for missing sessions. Fetch participants with registrations. Cancellation checks session first and atomically deletes only the matching session/registration pair; zero affected rows mean REGISTRATION_NOT_FOUND. Repeated cancellation is 404; capacity is freed and reinscription generates a new ID. Session deletion checks existence then registrations, rejects nonempty sessions with SESSION_HAS_REGISTRATIONS, and deletes by ID with row-count checking. Only fk_registrations_session violations are mapped to that conflict. Preserve coaches, participants and all unrelated registrations. No cascading deletion, migration or concurrency capacity change."
  }
